    "result_text": "Green. All three findings were correct and are now addressed:\n\n1. **Dead `matches`/parallel definition** \u2014 `RejectDuplicateIdentity` and `CountHouseholdMembers` now ask the domain question via `HouseholdKey.matches(existing)` instead of hashing both owners and string-comparing the 12-hex id. \"Same household\" has a single definition (`HouseholdKey.equals`), `matches`/`equals`/`hashCode` are live again, and SHA-256 is no longer computed per existing owner on every create.\n\n2. **Misleading data-dependency comments** \u2014 `AssignHousehold`'s Javadoc and the `owners.POST.yml` comment now state correctly that the stored id feeds `OwnerIdentity`/the DTO, and that the duplicate check and size count derive the household themselves rather than reading the stored value.\n\n3. **Minor** \u2014 `HouseholdKey.canonical()` dropped to `private` (only `householdId()` and `toString()` use it).\n\nAcceptance behaviour is unchanged and the suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).",
